From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Rowley <johnrowleyster@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 23:09:33 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(miniwin): fit the virtual display in a resizable window

The virtual display (the display mode, or the window's size when the
primary surface is made) is now fitted into the window whatever its size:
the largest rectangle of its aspect, centred, with black bars at the sides
or above and below. A resized window, or one made full screen at the
desktop's size, takes effect at the next Flip, between frames; a minimized
window keeps its target until it returns.

miniwin/miniwinpresentation.h states the fit (Miniwin_FitTransform, the
transform Direct3DRMDevice2Impl already computed) and its rules:
- The 3D device renders at the window's pixels by default, or at most at
  the virtual display's (Miniwin_SetRenderResolution), and the target is
  scaled to the swapchain when presented.
- A viewport covering the whole display widens into the bars, as before,
  unless Miniwin_SetViewportsFillWindow(false) keeps it to the display's
  aspect and fit; then Transform and InverseTransform agree with the
  picture at any window size.
- 2D images and viewport rectangles are clipped to the fit, so nothing is
  drawn into the bars.
- MINIWIN_DUMP_FRAME writes the picture at the resolution it was drawn at.

The SDL GPU backend also releases its download buffer when it resizes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

